Verify Your Implementation
Before submitting, walk through these verification scenarios to confirm your work is complete.
Verification 1 — Data completeness Open each of your four datasets and confirm the row counts and column counts match your expectations. The unified dataset should have more rows than any individual source (due to joins). If the row count seems unexpectedly high, review your join type and consider whether fan-out is occurring as expected.
Verification 2 — Dashboard interactivity Open your published dashboard. On each sheet, apply a filter and confirm the visuals update. Click a data point to trigger one-click filtering on a second visual. Use the cross-sheet navigation action and confirm it takes you to the correct sheet.
Verification 3 — Quick Chat accuracy Open Quick Chat scoped to your Topic. Ask a question you know the answer to from your dashboard (e.g., "What is the total revenue from closed-won deals?"). Compare Q's answer to the KPI on your Sales Pipeline sheet. They should agree or you should be able to explain the discrepancy.
Verification 4 — Report completeness Review your executive report against the requirements: Does it cover data strategy, design rationale, Topic configuration effects, key insights with actions, and AI vs. dashboard comparison? Can a non-technical reader understand it without logging in?
Verification 5 — Annotation quality Review your dashboard annotations. Each should go beyond restating the chart title — it should include a specific number, a business explanation, and a recommended action.
